        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3e1ae44d-3e1d-5142-9c13-c41e94289ce5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Buddy Baker, Bill Bixby, Jack Clayton, Ray Bradbury, Richard M. Sherman, Robert B. Sherman, Paul J. Smith\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang, Something Wicked This Way Comes, The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again, The Shaggy D.A., The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh, The Fox and the Hound, Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree\n- Topics: film music, Disney films, California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- Buddy Baker was an American composer born on January 4, 1918, and he died on July 26, 2002.\n- Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree featured songs written by the Sherman Brothers, Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman, and its score was composed and conducted by Buddy Baker.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang follows slick gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is duped into caring for a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- In 1975, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang together with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1976, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Shaggy D.A. together with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1977, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh together with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1979, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again together with Paul J. Smith.\n- In 1981, Buddy Baker helped score the Disney film The Fox and the Hound together with Paul J. Smith.\n- Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay by Ray Bradbury based on his novel of the same name.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "505ed18c-3206-5abd-825f-71c2ff91918c",
        "text": "Page: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Something Wicked This Way Comes (film). Sentence: Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay written by Ray Bradbury, based on his novel of the same name.\nPage: Buddy Baker (composer). Sentence: Norman Dale \"Buddy\" Baker (January 4, 1918 – July 26, 2002) was an American composer who, together with Paul J. Smith, scored many Disney films, such as \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" in 1975, \"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again\" in 1979, \"The Shaggy D.A.\" in 1976, \"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh\" in 1977, and \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.\nPage: Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree. Sentence: Its songs were written by the Sherman Brothers (Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman) and the score was composed and conducted by Buddy Baker.",
